    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:18px; margin-bottom:2px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Roman',Times,serif;">PS&#151;12</font>
    </div>

<hr size='3' noshade width='100%' style='page-break-before: always;' >






    <div style="text-align:left; margin-bottom:8px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Roman',Times,serif;"><b>INFORMATION REGARDING THE REFERENCE ASSET</b></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-bottom:4px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Roman',Times,serif;"><b><u>Fidelity Dividends for Inflation Index PR</u></b></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">All information in this pricing supplement regarding the Fidelity Dividends for Inflation Index (the &#147;<b>Reference Asset</b>&#148;), including, without limitation, its make-up, method of calculation and changes in its components, has been derived from publicly available information, without independent verification. This information reflects the policies of, and is subject to change by, Fidelity Product Services LLC (&#147;<b>FPS</b>&#148;). FPS has appointed a third party, S&P Dow Jones Indices LLC (&#147;<b>S&P Dow Jones</b>&#148;), to calculate and publish theReference Asset. FPS has no obligation to publish, and may discontinue the publication of, the Reference Asset.&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The Reference Asset is designed to measure the performance of large- and mid-capitalization dividend-yielding stocks representing U.S. equity sectors that have tended to outperform in inflationary environments. No assurance can be provided that any U.S. equity sector will outperform at any time. Publication of the Reference Asset began in December 1995. The Reference Asset is reported by Bloomberg L.P. under the ticker symbol &#147;FIDUSDIP.&#148;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><b>Construction of the Reference Asset</b></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The construction of the Reference Asset begins with identifying the eligible investment universe (the &#147;<b>U.S. Investment Universe</b>&#148;). The U.S. Investment Universe consists of the largest 1,000 U.S. stocks(determined on the basis of free-float adjusted market capitalization, calculated as the combined market capitalization of all share classes for each stock) that meet the liquidity and investability requirements set forth below, excluding securities: (i) whose country is not defined as the U.S. as determined by reference to FactSet databases; (ii) whose security type is not set to common stock as determined by reference to FactSet databases; (iii) that are not the parent entity (where there is a parent entity listed in the United States), or that are not the child entity with the highest average daily dollar trading volume (where there are multiple child entities listed in the United States but no parent entity); and (iv) that are limited partnerships, business development companies, American depositary receipts, closed-end funds, unit investment trusts or mutual funds.</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The liquidity and investability requirements used to determine the securities in the U.S. Investment Universe are as follows:</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left;text-indent:-24px;padding-left:48px; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">(i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <i>Data Availability Screens:</i>To be eligible for inclusion in the U.S. Investment Universe, a security must have non-zero data with respect to price, market capitalization and trading volume available for a period of six months.&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left;text-indent:-72px;padding-left:96px; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left;text-indent:-30px;padding-left:48px; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">(ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <i>Liquidity and Investability Screens:</i> In order to be included in the U.S. Investment Universe, a security must have a free float-adjusted market capitalization that exceeds 15% and a three month average daily dollar trading volume that exceeds $100 million.&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Once the U.S. Investment Universe is defined, each security will be reclassified into one of the following four categories: Commodities, Pricing Power, Real Assets & Infrastructure and Other. These four categories are composed of the following Global Industry Classification Standard (&#147;<b>GICS</b><b><sup>&#174;</sup></b>&#148;) sectors & industries:&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

 <table style=" border-collapse:collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
<tr>
   <td width="0%" valign = "baseline">
    <div style ="text-indent:24px;margin-top:16px;"><font style="font-size:10pt;">&#9679;</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
    </div>

   </td>

   <td style="padding-top:4px;">
    <div style ="padding-left:4px;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:8px; text-align:left;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Commodities&#8212; Energy and Materials;&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

   </td>

  </tr>

</table>
 <table style=" border-collapse:collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
<tr>
   <td width="0%" valign = "baseline">
    <div style ="text-indent:24px;margin-top:8px;"><font style="font-size:10pt;">&#9679;</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
    </div>

   </td>

   <td style="padding-top:4px;">
    <div style ="padding-left:4px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:8px; text-align:left;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Pricing Power&nbsp;&#8212; Consumer Staples and Health Care;</font>
    </div>

   </td>

  </tr>

</table>
 <table style=" border-collapse:collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
<tr>
   <td width="0%" valign = "baseline">
    <div style ="text-indent:24px;margin-top:8px;"><font style="font-size:10pt;">&#9679;</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
    </div>

   </td>

   <td style="padding-top:4px;">
    <div style ="padding-left:4px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:8px; text-align:left;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Real Assets & Infrastructure &#8212; Real Estate, Utilities, Airport Services (Industrials), Highways & Rail tracks (Industrials), Railroads (Industrials), Alternative Carriers (Communication Services), Cable & Satellite (Communication Services), Integrated Telecom Services (Communication Services) and Marine Ports & Services (Industrials); and&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

   </td>

  </tr>

</table>
 <table style=" border-collapse:collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
<tr>
   <td width="0%" valign = "baseline">
    <div style ="text-indent:24px;margin-top:8px;"><font style="font-size:10pt;">&#9679;</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
    </div>

   </td>

   <td style="padding-top:4px;">
    <div style ="padding-left:4px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:2px; text-align:left;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Other &#8212; Communication Services (remove industries listed above), Consumer Discretionary Financials, Industrials (remove industries listed above) and Information Technology.</font>
    </div>

   </td>

  </tr>

</table>


    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:18px; margin-bottom:2px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Roman',Times,serif;">PS&#151;13</font>
    </div>

<hr size='3' noshade width='100%' style='page-break-before: always;' >






    <div style="text-align:left; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">For each stock in the U.S. Investment Universe, a weighted-average score will be calculated to evaluate each stock based on the weighted dividend factors set forth in the chart below (a &#147;<b>composite factor score</b>&#148;).</font>
    </div>

 <table  width="70%"  cellpadding = "0"  cellspacing = ".0"  style = " border-collapse:collapse; " >
  <tr>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="14%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-top:1px solid #000000; border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Dividend Yield</font>
    </div>

   </td>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="7%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-top:1px solid #000000; border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left;padding-left:8px; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">70%</font>
    </div>

   </td>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="45%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-top:1px solid #000000; border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left;padding-left:5px; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Trailing dividend over last twelve months over price per share</font>
    </div>

   </td>

  </tr>

  <tr>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="14%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Payout Ratio</font>
    </div>

   </td>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="7%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left;padding-left:8px; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">15%</font>
    </div>

   </td>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="45%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left;padding-left:5px; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Trailing dividends over last twelve months over earnings per share</font>
    </div>

   </td>

  </tr>

  <tr>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="14%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Dividend Growth</font>
    </div>

   </td>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="7%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left;padding-left:8px; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">15%</font>
    </div>

   </td>

   <td  colspan="1"  width="45%"  rowspan="1"  valign="top"  style = "border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; padding-top:1.5px ;padding-left:2.8px ;padding-right:4.5px ; " >
    <div style="text-align:left;padding-left:5px; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">Trailing dividends over last twelve months over dividends from one year ago</font>
    </div>

   </td>

  </tr>

</table>
    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The process for calculating each stock&#8217;s composite factor score involves first comparing the distribution of a given stock with respect to each of the above factors separately within each sector (using a statistical measure known as a &#147;<b>z-score</b>&#148;). For each security, the z-score with respect to each factor is then weighted according to the chart set forth above and summed to compute a weighted average factor score. The composite factor score for each security is determined based on the z-score of each stock&#8217;s weighted average factor score, which compares the distribution of a stock&#8217;s weighted average factor score to the mean within the relevant sector.</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The composite factor scores are then adjusted in order to target securities for inclusion in the Reference Asset that would result in a smaller weighted average market capitalization than the U.S. Investment Universe. The adjustment to each composite factor score is determined based on the z-score of each stock&#8217;s market capitalization, which compares the distribution of a stock&#8217;s market capitalization to the mean within the U.S. Investment Universe (a &#147;<b>size z-score</b>&#148;). The size z-scores are added to the composite factor scores until the adjustment to each composite factor score results in the selection of stocks with a weighted average market capitalization that is 0.5 standard deviations below that of the U.S. Investment Universe.</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The stocks within each of the following five groups (each, a &#147;<b>represented sector</b>&#148;) are then ranked within their respective represented sector according to their size-adjusted composite factor scores, and the highest-scored stocks within each represented sector are selected for inclusion in the Reference Asset: (i) Energy; (ii) Materials; (iii) Consumer Staples; (iv) Health Care; and (v) Real Estate, Utilities, Airport Services (Industrials), Highways & Rail tracks (Industrials), Railroads (Industrials), Alternative Carriers (Communication Services), Cable & Satellite (Communication Services), Integrated Telecom Services (Communication Services) and Marine Ports & Services (Industrials).&nbsp;The stock selection process targets approximately 50 total constituents for inclusion in the Reference Asset consisting of the top-ranked stocks within each represented sector, selected using a methodology that will select the number of stocks in each sector based on the weight of each sector as determined by the redistributed sector weights as further described below. This results in each sector having a number of constituents proportional to the sector&#8217;s weight in the Reference Asset. The final constituent count may be more or less than 50 due to corporate actions. No stocks are selected from the &#147;Other&#148; category in order to emphasize represented sectors that have tended to outperform during inflationary periods.</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The weight assigned to each represented sector will be equal to its weight in the broader U.S. equity market, plus an overweight adjustment equal to 1/5 of the weight in the broader U.S. equity market of the &#147;Other&#148; category.&#160; The weights of the stocks within each represented sector will be proportional to their market capitalization, subject to the overweight adjustment for that represented sector, which be allocated equally among the stocks within that represented sector. The purpose of adding the overweight adjustment equally to the stocks within each represented sector is to reduce the potential for concentration in certain stocks based solely on market capitalization. If necessary, the final portfolio will be rescaled to 100%.&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><b>Calculation of the Reference Asset</b></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><b>&nbsp;</b></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; margin-bottom:13px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">TheReference Asset is calculated by means of the divisor methodology in which the index value is equal to the quotient of the total available market capitalization of the constituents and the divisor. In order to maintain the continuity of the index value in the event of certain changes due to non-market factors affecting the constituents, the divisor is adjusted as part of the rebalancing of the Reference Asset.</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><b>Maintenance of the Reference Asset</b></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><i>&nbsp;</i></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><i>Rebalancing&nbsp;</i></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><i>&nbsp;</i></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The Reference Asset is rebalanced semi-annually on the third Friday of each February and August, effective as of the following market open. The Reference Asset observes the data needed to make the above determinations on the date that is 10 business days prior to the rebalancing date.</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><b>&nbsp;</b></font>
    </div>



    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:2px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Roman',Times,serif;">PS&#151;14</font>
    </div>

<hr size='3' noshade width='100%' style='page-break-before: always;' >


    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><i>Ongoing Maintenance&nbsp;</i></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;"><i>&nbsp;</i></font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:justify; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">The Reference Asset is also reviewed on an ongoing basis to account for corporate events such as mergers, takeovers, delistings, group changes, suspensions, spin-offs/demergers or bankruptcies. Changes to index composition and related weight adjustments are made as soon as they are effective. Corporate actions will be treated as follows:&nbsp;</font>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:left; border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">&nbsp;</font>
    </div>



    <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:2px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Roman',Times,serif;">PS&#151;15</font>
    </div>

