    <div style="text-align:left;padding-left:16px; margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;border-width:1px 1px 1px 1px; border-style:none none none none;"><font style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Times New Romans',Times,serif;">In the event that S&P Dow Jones applies the event as a non-zero price spin-off event, the spun-off company is added to the index with respect to spinoff ratio. The spot price of the underlying security is adjusted after market close of the day prior to the ex-date by the closing spot price of the spun off company multiplied by the spinoff ratio, thus making it a market cap neutral event. The divisor will not be adjusted.</font>
